course: dictionary
lesson: 4346
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word guide can be a person, a book, or an action. Ask yourself what job the word does in the sentence: is it a thing, a person, or something someone does?
explain: «Picture a blind woman walking to the shops: her guide dog stops dead at the kerb so she knows a road is there.» Here guide is a noun for a helper who leads the way. Try swapping in helper: the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: «Sleepwalking happens in deep sleep... so it is best to guide them gently back to bed.» Now guide is a verb, an action: to lead someone along a path. The words gently back to bed show what the guiding does, so the context makes the meaning clear.
fact: A guide is a person who shows people the way or shows them around a place, like a tour guide.
fact: As a verb, guide means to show someone the way or lead them.
fact: A guide can also be a book, map or set of information that helps you learn about something, like a guide to birds.
fact: A rough guide is something that helps you judge, but it is not exact.
fact: Guides can also mean Girl Guides, a club for girls like Scouts.
exercise: «Her guide dog stops dead at the kerb so she knows a road is there.» What does guide dog mean? | *A dog that helps a blind person | A dog that runs in races | A dog that barks at cars
exercise: Maya reads «a guide to birds» in the library. What is the guide here? | *A book that helps you learn about birds | A person who walks birdwatchers around a park | A club for girls like Scouts
exercise: «...so it is best to guide them gently back to bed.» In this sentence, what does guide mean? | To sleep deeply | To draw straight lines | *To lead someone, showing them the way | To be a member of a club
test: Jayden says, «Guide lines help you draw straight.» In maths and art, what is a guide line? | A line painted on a road for cars | A line of people waiting in a queue | *A line that helps you draw neatly and straight
test: «Advice on a pet-shop label isn't always the best; animal charities and vets give care guides.» Here guide means: | *A book or set of information that helps you care for animals | To lead someone by the hand | A person who leads a tour
exam: Ella reads «guides count caimans by pairs of glowing eyes» and asks who the guides are. | *People who lead and show others the way, such as a boat guide | Shiny layers behind the eye | Pairs of glowing eyes | Children counting in a classroom
